# 📌 Project Explanation

This project was developed to simulate a real-world business reporting scenario where raw transactional sales data needed to be transformed into a structured analytical solution for performance monitoring and decision-making.

The complete workflow was built entirely in Microsoft Excel by combining Power Query, Data Modelling, DAX calculations, and dashboard reporting into a single integrated solution.

Instead of performing static analysis, the project focused on creating a scalable and interactive reporting system capable of answering critical business questions related to:

- Revenue growth
- Product profitability
- Seasonal demand
- Sales behaviour
- Inventory performance
- Operational efficiency

A structured analytical approach was followed throughout the project:

- Raw transactional data was cleaned and transformed using Power Query
- Relationships were designed through a Star Schema Data Model
- KPI calculations were created using DAX measures
- Pivot-based reporting was implemented for dynamic analysis
- Interactive dashboards were designed for executive-level reporting

Special attention was given to building reusable analytical components such as:

- Custom Date dimensions
- Time intelligence calculations
- Dynamic filtering
- KPI-driven reporting
- Interactive visualizations

The project demonstrates how Excel can be used as a complete Business Intelligence platform for building scalable reporting solutions without external BI tools.

This analysis ultimately helped identify:
- High-performing product categories
- Seasonal sales trends
- Revenue concentration patterns
- Inventory optimization opportunities
- Profitability behaviour across time periods

The project reflects practical skills in:
- ETL workflows
- Data modelling
- Business Intelligence reporting
- DAX logic development
- Dashboard engineering
- Analytical storytelling
